    {
      "id": "s02-carrier-equation",
      "intent": "The carrier equation separates dense feature creation from token-preserving window partitioning.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into the dense feature field F. The field remains spatial, so the carrier is not reduced to one compact state. The window operator partitions F into X while keeping every token. The equation defines the carrier path that the compact thought process reads and updates.",
